ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: red
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "vLLM", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/configuration/optimization.html#chunked-prefill", overlap: "Shipping chunked prefill/continuous batching baseline: splits prefills and batches them with decode; does not semantically commit next reasoning on partial tool-result content."},
  {system: "SGLang", url: "https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/server_arguments", overlap: "Shipping chunked prefill controls (`--chunked-prefill-size`, dynamic chunking); overlap is scheduler/prefill latency hiding, not correctness-risky partial tool-result commit."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/features/paged-attention-ifb-scheduler.html", overlap: "Shipping in-flight batching and chunked context: context phase can execute with generation phase; not semantic early-commit on partial external tool results."},
  {system: "LLMCompiler", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.04511", overlap: "Parallelizes independent function calls at call-graph level; captures inter-call latency without redo risk, but does not consume partial streaming tool results."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold at realistic workload in the supplied gate. EXP-0038 reports N=1641 real tool-result records with median rho 0.007-0.508 for realistic classes, 0-9.1% clearing rho>=1, and search_rag collapsing to 0% rho>=1 under realistic next-step lengths. The only class with apparent rho headroom is also not end-front-loaded (%END<=0.30 = 5.5%) and is truncation-resistant, so the mechanism pays exactly where it is likely to commit wrong. For api/code/db/web, N=512 truncation captures actionable content at 100%, and shipping chunked/in-flight prefill systems already address most residual prefill latency.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. This is not a systems insight/design win on the evidence; it is a plausible mechanism whose operating regime is empirically absent. The packet’s kill criteria fire independently: rho<1 for dominant classes, dumb truncation matches actionable content for 4/5 classes, and the high-rho case is adversarial on f_fl. OSS search found mature shipping prefill/scheduler overlap in vLLM, SGLang, and TensorRT-LLM, but no exact correctness-safe semantic commit on partial streaming tool RESULT. That absence does not rescue the claim because EXP-0038 shows insufficient addressable latency and poor correctness conditions at realistic scale. Reproducibility is acceptable for a kill gate: pre-registered PRE_REG.md, scripts, records.json/per_record.csv/counts/analysis paths are given.
